/* ======================================================================
   One measured gait cycle per subject, with the RAW surface EMG recorded
   during the same stride.

   Lencioni T, Carpinella I, Rabuffetti M, Marzegan A, Ferrarin M (2019)
   "Human kinematic, kinetic and EMG data during different walking and
   stair ascending and descending tasks", Scientific Data 6:309.
   doi:10.6084/m9.figshare.c.4494755, CC BY 4.0.

   Per subject: one level-walking trial, heel strike to heel strike.
     - markers  : 20 sagittal joint centres per frame, in centimetres,
                  x zeroed at the first pelvis position.  Hip centres are
                  the ASIS markers dropped 85 mm; everything else is a
                  marker as recorded.
     - EMG      : five channels, RAW, in microvolts, at the rate in `fs`.
                  The constant amplifier offset has been subtracted and
                  nothing else has been done to them -- no rectification,
                  no filtering beyond the 10-400 Hz analogue band-pass the
                  authors applied before sampling.

   The trial chosen for each subject is the one whose linear envelope best
   matches that subject's mean across their normal-speed walking trials.
   ====================================================================== */
